SLEEP(1)                       P32W Unix                        SLEEP(1)

NAME
       sleep - suspend execution for an interval

SYNOPSIS
       sleep seconds

DESCRIPTION
       sleep waits for the given whole number of seconds and then
       exits. It is used to run a command after a delay, or between
       repetitions of one.

EXAMPLES
       sleep 60; echo tea ready      wait a minute first
       while true; do date; sleep 10; done

EXIT STATUS
       0; 2 with no argument, more than one, or one that is not a
       whole number of seconds from 0 to 2147483647 ("usage: sleep
       seconds", "sleep: 1.5: not a number of seconds").

SEE ALSO
       sh(1), at(1), alarm(2)

BUGS
       Fractions are not allowed, and the wait may be up to a
       second short, since it ends when the seconds counter reaches
       the target.
